{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-num-12-1","title":"Numbers 12:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God rebukes the sedition of Miriam and Aaron. 11 Miriam's leprosy is healed at the prayer of Moses. 14 God commands her to be shut out of the host. 16 The people encamp in the wilderness of Paran.</p>\n<p>Miriam. Mt 10:36; 12:48; Joh 7:5; 15:20; Ga 4:16 Ethiopian. or, Cushite. Ex 2:16,21 married. Heb. taken. Ge 24:3,37; 26:34,35; 27:46; 28:6-9; 34:14,15; 41:45; Ex 34:16 Le 21:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-2","title":"Numbers 12:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Hath the Lord. 16:3; Ex 4:30; 5:1; 7:10; 15:20,21; Mic 6:4 hath he not. 11:29; Pr 13:10; Ro 12:3,10; Php 2:3,14; 1Pe 5:5 And the. 11:1; Ge 29:33; 2Sa 11:27; 2Ki 19:4; Ps 94:7-9; Isa 37:4 Eze 35:12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-3","title":"Numbers 12:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>very. Ps 147:6; 149:4; Mt 5:5; 11:29; 21:5; 2Co 10:1; 1Th 2:7; Jas 3:13 1Pe 3:4 above. 11:10-15; 20:10-12; Ps 106:32,33; 2Co 11:5; 12:11; Jas 3:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-4","title":"Numbers 12:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the Lord. Ps 76:9 Come out. 16:16-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-5","title":"Numbers 12:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>11:25; Ex 34:5; 40:38; Ps 99:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-6","title":"Numbers 12:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>a prophet. Ge 20:7; Ex 7:1; Ps 105:15; Mt 23:31,34,37; Lu 20:6; Eph 4:11 Re 11:3,10 in a vision. Ge 15:1; 46:2; Job 4:13; 33:15; Ps 89:19; Eze 1:1; Da 8:2 Da 10:8,16,17; Lu 1:11,22; Ac 10:11,17; 22:17,18 a dream. Ge 31:10,11; 1Ki 3:5; Jer 23:28; Da 7:1; Mt 1:20; 2:12,13,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-7","title":"Numbers 12:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>My servant. De 18:18; Ps 105:26; Mt 11:9,11; Ac 3:22,23; 7:31 faithful. 1Co 4:2; 1Ti 3:15; Heb 3:2-6; 1Pe 2:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-8","title":"Numbers 12:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>mouth. 14:14; Ex 33:11; De 34:10; 1Ti 6:16 dark speeches. Ps 49:4; Eze 17:2; 20:49; Mt 13:35; Joh 15:15; 1Co 13:12 similitude. Ex 24:10,11; 33:19,23; 34:5-7; De 4:15; Isa 40:18; 46:5; Joh 1:18 Joh 14:7-10; 15:24; 2Co 3:18; 4:4-6; Col 1:15; Heb 1:3 were ye. Ex 34:30; Lu 10:16; 1Th 4:8; 2Pe 2:10; Jude 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-9","title":"Numbers 12:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>11:1; Ho 5:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-10","title":"Numbers 12:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>the cloud. Ex 33:7-10; Eze 10:4,5,18,19; Ho 9:12; Mt 25:41 behold. De 24:9 leprous. Le 13:2,3-46; 2Ki 5:27; 15:5; 2Ch 26:19-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-11","title":"Numbers 12:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>I beseech thee. Ex 12:32; 1Sa 2:30; 12:19; 15:24,25; 1Ki 13:6; Jer 42:2; Ac 8:24 Re 3:9 lay not. 2Sa 19:19; 24:10; 2Ch 16:9; Ps 38:1-5; Pr 30:32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-12","title":"Numbers 12:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>as one dead. Ps 88:4,5; Eph 2:1-5; Col 2:13; 1Ti 5:6 of whom. Job 3:16; Ps 58:8; 1Co 15:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-13","title":"Numbers 12:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>14:2,13-20; 16:41,46-50; Ex 32:10-14; 1Sa 12:23; 15:11; Mt 5:44,45 Lu 6:28; 23:34; Ac 7:60; Ro 12:21; Jas 5:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-14","title":"Numbers 12:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>spit. De 25:9; Job 30:10; Isa 50:6; Mt 26:67; Heb 12:9 let her be. 5:2,3; Le 13:45,46; 14:8; 2Ch 26:20,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-15","title":"Numbers 12:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>shut out. De 24:8,9 and the. Ge 9:21-23; Ex 20:12 till Miriam. La 3:32; Mic 6:4; 7:8,9; Hab 3:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-num-12-16","title":"Numbers 12:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"NUM","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>afterward. 11:35; 33:18 Hazeroth.The exact situation of this place is unknown. Dr. Shaw computes it to be three days' journey, i.e., thirty miles from Sinai. From this passage, it appears that the wilderness of Paran commenced immediately upon their leaving this station. Calmet observes, that there is a town called Hazor in Arabia Petr�a, in all probability the same as Hazerim, the ancient habitation of the Hivites (De 2:23); and likewise, according to all appearances, the Hazeroth, where the Hebrews encamped.</p>\n<p>the wilderness. 10:12; 13:3,26; Ge 21:21; 1Sa 25:1; Hab 3:3</p>"}]}